# Strangers for Mary website: rules for every session


This Next.js version has breaking changes (see Website/web/AGENTS.md). Read the guides in `Website/web/node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing routing, data fetching, caching or route handler code.

This is the pre-launch website for Strangers for Mary. The design and copy are approved; keep them as they are. The app is `Website/web/`. The full brief is in `Website/sfm-website-build-kit/prompts/02-nextjs-website.md` and the backend contract in `Website/sfm-website-build-kit/prompts/01-apps-script-backend.md`.

## Never

- Never redraw, retrace, recolour or retype the logo, mark or wordmark. Use the SVGs in `public/brand/` through the `Logo` and `Mark` components.
- Never redraw or approximate the brand pattern. It appears in one place only: the lime pattern at 10% on the dark closing card. Never add it to the header, footer, section backgrounds or lime panels.
- Never hard-code a user-facing string in a component. Every word lives in `src/content/strings.ts`, transcribed from `Website/sfm-website-build-kit/content/strings-master.md` without rewording.
- Never hard-code a colour, font, spacing value, radius, shadow or breakpoint. Every design value lives in `src/styles/tokens/tokens.ts`; SCSS uses the generated CSS variables and mixins.
- Never edit `*.generated.*` files; run `npm run tokens` instead.
- Never use inline `style` props, arbitrary Tailwind values, or Tailwind colour and spacing utilities inside a component that has an SCSS module.
- Never import upward or sideways between layers (`app` → `views` → `widgets` → `features` → `entities` → `shared`).
- Never expose `APPS_SCRIPT_SECRET` or call the Apps Script URL from the browser.
- Never add a runtime dependency without asking.
- Never use a photo that is not in `public/images/` (copied from the kit's `assets/photos/`, all from the Stock Images folder). No stock, AI-generated or placeholder images; ask for a Stock Images file instead.

## Always

- Put route-level composition in `src/views/<Page>/`, with page-only sections in `src/views/<Page>/sections/<Section>/`. Each component has `Component.tsx`, `Component.module.scss` and `index.ts`.
- Reuse `src/shared/ui` components before writing new markup. If two pages need the same piece, move it down to `shared` (or `widgets` if it is a large block).
- Use `useTheme()`, `useFonts()`, `useStrings()` and `useBreakpoint()` when JavaScript needs a design value or a string.
- Build mobile-first at the breakpoints in `tokens.ts` (640, 1024, 1280, 1536). Below 1024px the header shows the mark only (never the full logo), "Join us" and the menu button; see `prompts/03-responsive-header-and-menu.md`.
- Keep Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only for interaction.
- Match the design reference in `Website/sfm-website-build-kit/design-reference/` pixel for pixel at 390, 768, 1280 and 1440px.

## Copy rules

- No em dashes. No exclamation marks in headlines.
- The word "pillar" never appears on the site.
- Strangers for Mary is a "network", never a "family".
- Headlines are sentence case and two-tone (main clause ink, second clause muted).
- "PASS IT ON." next to the logo or mark is Barlow Condensed 500 with wide letter-spacing, never Nohemi Bold.

## Design rules

- Pages sit on neutral grounds (paper, white, mistTint). Colour lives on a few elements: at most one large lime element per screen, and one ink card per page (the closing card).
- Sections are separated by space, not colour bands.
- Lime is never used for text on light grounds.

## Before finishing any task

- `npm run lint`, `npm run lint:styles`, `npm run test` and `npm run build` pass.
- New strings are in `strings.ts`, new values in `tokens.ts`.
- Say what changed and anything that differs from the design reference.
